{"type":"message","id":"0e93c923","parentId":"a8890048","timestamp":"2026-05-21T11:40:59.476Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_GD83oYVkvR9CybiBrdIQtYud","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"run_id\": \"20260521-113332\",\n  \"collected_at\": \"2026-05-21T11:40:30Z\",\n  \"selected_event\": {\n    \"title\": \"SEC opens public input on prediction market ETFs as Polymarket expands event contracts\",\n    \"date\": \"2026-05-20/2026-05-21\",\n    \"why_this_is_the_biggest_event\": \"It is the most consequential cross-feed crypto story in the sampled RSS set: it appears in multiple feeds, involves both the SEC and CFTC, touches regulated prediction markets and ETFs, and has market-structure implications beyond a single token or company announcement.\"\n  },\n  \"summary\": \"On May 20-21, 2026, the SEC said it is seeking public feedback on prediction market ETFs and other novel ETFs, while Polymarket filed to list U.S. parlays/combinatorial outcome contracts no earlier than May 21. Together, the developments signal growing institutionalization of prediction markets and renewed scrutiny over how event contracts should be regulated.\",\n  \"cross_references\": [\n    {\n      \"source_name\": \"CoinDesk RSS\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss\",\n      \"matched_items\": [\n        {\n          \"headline\": \"Polymarket moves to list parlays while SEC seeks public input on prediction market ETFs\",\n          \"url\": \"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/05/20/polymarket-moves-to-list-parlays-while-sec-seeks-public-input-on-prediction-market-etfs\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_name\": \"Cointelegraph RSS\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://cointelegraph.com/rss\",\n      \"matched_items\": [\n        {\n          \"headline\": \"SEC Seeks Feedback on Prediction Markets ETFs\",\n          \"url\": \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-seeks-public-comment-as-it-weighs-prediction-market-etfs\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_name\": \"SEC statement\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sec.gov/newsroom/speeches-statements/atkins-statement-novel-exchange-traded-funds-052026\",\n      \"matched_items\": [\n        {\n          \"headline\": \"Statement on Novel Exchange-Traded Funds (ETFs)\",\n          \"url\": \"https://www.sec.gov/newsroom/speeches-statements/atkins-statement-novel-exchange-traded-funds-052026\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"deep_facts\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"SEC Chair Paul Atkins said ETFs remain a major driver of innovation in securities markets and that ETF assets have tripled since 2019.\",\n      \"source\": \"SEC statement\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Atkins said novel products raise novel questions and instructed SEC staff to seek public input on how the Commission should respond to recent market changes, including event contract ETFs.\",\n      \"source\": \"SEC statement\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Polymarket filed a self-certification to list 'combinatorial outcome contracts' (parlays) in U.S. sports event contracts, stating the exchange could list them no earlier than May 21, 2026.\",\n      \"source\": \"CoinDesk\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Under Polymarket's filing, every leg in the parlay must resolve successfully for the contract to pay $1.00; if any single leg fails, the contract resolves to $0.00.\",\n      \"source\": \"CoinDesk\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Cointelegraph reported that Bitwise filed in February for PredictionShares ETFs tracking U.S. election results, and Roundhill Investments and GraniteShares also filed for prediction market ETFs.\",\n      \"source\": \"Cointelegraph\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Cointelegraph said prediction markets now consistently exceed $15 billion in monthly trading volume across sports, elections, financial results, and cultural events.\",\n      \"source\": \"Cointelegraph\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The policy backdrop is a jurisdictional tension: the CFTC oversees event contracts at the federal level, while state regulators and gambling firms argue sports prediction markets infringe on states' rights to regulate and tax gambling products.\",\n      \"source\": \"CoinDesk\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The CoinDesk article notes that lawmakers are reviewing prediction markets and the issue is likely to remain in litigation and regulatory focus.\",\n      \"source\": \"CoinDesk\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"event_details\": {\n    \"regulatory_bodies\": [\"SEC\", \"CFTC\"],\n    \"market_segment\": [\"prediction markets\", \"event contracts\", \"ETFs\"],\n    \"key_entities\": [\"Polymarket\", \"Bitwise\", \"Roundhill Investments\", \"GraniteShares\", \"Paul Atkins\"],\n    \"key_dates\": [\n\n[24 more lines in file. Use offset=81 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779363659475}}
